window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>The Forest Hides More than Magic.</p> <p>She was supposed to plan a wedding. Instead, she stepped into a cursed kingdom.</p> <p>Gabby has always preferred books to reality—especially when reality means an unwanted engagement and a future she didn’t choose. But after a bitter argument with her ailing father, she returns home to find him being taken by strangers into the forest no one dares enter.</p> <p>The dark forest marks the boundary between her world and another—one steeped in secrets and long-buried magic. When Gabby learns her father is being forced to repay an old debt in a hidden kingdom, she makes an impossible choice: offer herself in his place.</p> <p>Now bound to a mysterious palace beyond the trees, Gabby finds herself at the mercy of a cold, enigmatic prince and a bargain she barely understands. As she adjusts to a life ruled by ancient magic, she begins to uncover truths that don’t match the fairy tales she once loved.</p> <p>Her story isn’t the only one unfolding—and some endings were never meant to be happy.</p> <p><i>As the Petal Falls</i>, this twisted <i>Beauty and the Beast</i> retelling begins an epic fantasy series where familiar stories intertwine, secrets run deep, and the forest never forgets.</p>"; 
